Report the probabilities of the tokens a grammar allows.

A grammar decides what is written. It does not decide what is reported, and
neither of the two existing readouts gives a caller the distribution over the
answers it constrained the model to:

  post_sampling_probs false  the softmax over the whole vocabulary, taken
                             before the sampler. The grammar is not in it, so
                             a caller has to pick an n_probs large enough to
                             catch its own answers and renormalise by hand -
                             and when the model wanted to write something
                             else, the answers are not in the top n at all.

  post_sampling_probs true   after the sampling chain, where the grammar and
                             the sampler have already chosen. One token is
                             left, at 1.0. On the OpenAI chat route nothing
                             comes back at all.

`grammar_probs` adds the one in between: apply only the grammar to the
pre-sampler softmax, and report every token that survives, scaled to sum to
one. The grammar allows a handful of tokens for a classification, so they all
fit and n_probs does not enter into it.

`grammar_mass` goes with them: what those tokens held before the scaling. It
is the difference between an answer and a letter the grammar forced out of a
model that was going to write something else, which the scaled numbers alone
cannot show. Measured on Qwen3-0.6B with one prompt, changing nothing but the
chat template's thinking flag: 0.000000 with thinking on, 0.999618 with it
off. Both wrote the same letter, and both looked like confident answers.

The readout also moves above common_sampler_accept. Accepting advances the
grammar past the token just chosen, so applying the grammar after it answers
"what may follow the answer" - for a one-token grammar, end of string. Only
counters sit between the two.

Three gates on n_probs had to learn about a request that asks for none: the
call to populate_token_probs, and the partial and final result builders.

